+/* 0138: 0137 gated sending on usbmuxd's advertised receive window, parsed
+ * from th_win on its ACKs under the assumption that it uses the same >>8
+ * wire convention as our own outbound window (0123/0135). In practice this
+ * stalled every loopback connection outright, syslog included - usbmuxd's
+ * synthetic TCP shim does not seem to advertise a real, growing window on
+ * this path at all ("usbmuxd does not check sequence numbers" was already
+ * the working assumption elsewhere in this file), so the parsed window
+ * stayed at (or decoded to) zero forever and nothing was ever allowed to
+ * send again. Rather than trust that field, throttle the dumb but reliable
+ * way: cap how many chunks a single ru_loop_poll_slot() call forwards, and
+ * let the very frequent outer poll loop (ru_tx_poll/ru_rx_poll/ru_loop_poll
+ * run every pass of the USB driver's main loop) spread a fast producer's
+ * output across many ticks instead of draining the whole socket backlog in
+ * one tight inner loop, which is what overran usbmuxd's small
+ * per-connection buffer in the first place ("Input buffer overflow ...
+ * space=891, payload=1075"). acked_seq/peer_window (0137) are still updated
+ * for visibility but no longer gate sending. */
+#define RU_LOOP_CHUNKS_PER_TICK 2u
 
